* Test circuit for the solver's MOSFET (tools/spice/cases/cmos.py; docs/circuit/solver-mosfet.md),
* not a part of the TR-909: one 4011UB NAND gate (models.cir's 4011UB_P, two in parallel from
* +5 V, and 4011UB_N, two in series), inputs a and b, its output into 10 nF to ground and 10k to
* 2.5 V (two 20k). The node between the two NMOS is tied to the rest only through them.
* Inputs: a, b (volts). Outputs: out, mid (the NMOS pair's middle).
Vdd vdd 0 5
Va a 0 input a
Vb b 0 input b
MPA out a vdd 4011UB_P
MPB out b vdd 4011UB_P
MNA out a mid 4011UB_N
MNB mid b 0 4011UB_N
CL out 0 10n
RLP out vdd 20k
RLN out 0 20k
.output out out
.output mid mid
